Check order matches CLAUDE.md's own listed order ("409 if not paused, no budget left, or end date passed"). No check against `start_date` — a paused campaign can resume into `active` even with a future `start_date`; the impression endpoint's own live date check is what actually gates whether impressions are accepted, exactly per the domain decision that correctness never depends on status alone.

`handlers.go`: `Resume`, same thin shape. `main.go`: `mux.HandleFunc("POST /campaigns/{id}/resume", h.Resume)`.

## `GET /stats/{id}` — plain read, no new mechanism

CLAUDE.md's spec: *"impressions, spent, remaining, budget, status"* — a distinct, smaller shape than the full `Campaign` JSON (no title/dates/timestamps). Since "impressions are derived from spent, not stored as a separate counter" (existing domain decision), `impressions` is just `spent` under a different name — no new repository method needed at all, this is a pure reshape of what `GetByID` already returns.

**`campaign.go`**:
```go
type Stats struct {
    Impressions int64  `json:"impressions"`
    Spent       int64  `json:"spent"`
    Remaining   int64  `json:"remaining"`
    Budget      int64  `json:"budget"`
    Status      string `json:"status"`
}

func (c Campaign) Stats() Stats {
    return Stats{
        Impressions: c.Spent,
        Spent:       c.Spent,
        Remaining:   c.Budget - c.Spent,
        Budget:      c.Budget,
        Status:      c.Status,
    }
}
```

**`service.go`**:
```go
func (s *Service) Stats(ctx context.Context, id int64) (Stats, error) {
    c, err := s.repo.GetByID(ctx, id)
    if errors.Is(err, pgx.ErrNoRows) {
        return Stats{}, httpx.NotFound("campaign not found")
    }
    if err != nil {
        return Stats{}, err
    }
    return c.Stats(), nil
}
```

**`handlers.go`**: `Stats`, same id-parsing shape, `200 OK` with the `Stats` body (not the full campaign).

**`main.go`**: `mux.HandleFunc("GET /stats/{id}", h.Stats)` — top-level path, matching `/impression/{id}`'s pattern, not nested under `/campaigns`.

## No new dependencies
Same stdlib + existing `pgx/v5`/`pgxpool`.

## CLAUDE.md update
Update the Hard Rules line currently reading *"Resuming a campaign still needs this same treatment... when we get there"* to record the decision, mirroring how the impression/budget-decrease lines were updated earlier.

